    "secondaryGap": "single-SOURCE (kaikki + wikipron are both Wiktionary-derived → correlated, not independent). The referee is DICTIONARY-shaped: it over-samples rare Latinate inflections (absorberende…) whose non-initial lexical stress a first-syllable rule engine can't recover, so the raw uniform % is deflated — the FREQUENCY-WEIGHTED metric (freq/nb.txt) is the real-text signal (~62%, in line with sv/nl). The broad transcription also carries pitch accent + length + a mixed rhotic (East retroflex ~ West/Bergen uvular), folded here.",
    "folds": [
        { "pattern": "[¹²]", "replace": "", "note": "PITCH ACCENT (tonelag 1 / 2) — the referee's superscript tone marker; lexical + unwritten → deferred, fold" },
        { "pattern": "ʁ", "replace": "ɾ", "note": "⟨r⟩: the referee mixes the East-Norwegian tap ɾ with the West/Bergen uvular ʁ (Arendal→ɑːɳ̩dɑːl ~ ɑːʁn̩dɑːl); we emit the tap → fold ʁ→ɾ" },
        { "pattern": "r", "replace": "ɾ", "note": "⟨r⟩ trill r ~ tap ɾ written inconsistently → fold to ɾ" },
        { "pattern": "ɑ", "replace": "a", "note": "the low vowel ⟨a⟩: one phoneme /ɑ/ written [a] (1865×) ~ [ɑ] (730×) — we emit back ɑ, the referee mostly front a → fold ɑ→a" }
